## Print / diagnostic catalog extensions

- GET|POST /api/admin/diagnostic-catalog/imaging-phrases, PATCH|DELETE .../[id]
- GET /api/imaging-phrases (ops phrase picker)
- Analyte section / valueType / AnalyteValueOption via analytes admin API
- ADR: docs/adr/clinic-print-forms.md
- Print checkup (`/print/checkup/[patientId]`) includes episode ICD diagnoses (`print-checkup.service`); default sections = Nafta intake 4 (`therapist` / `gynecologist` / `cardiologist` / `usm`)
- Visit exam print: `/print/visit-exam/[cpoeEntryId]` (`print-visit-exam.service`) — one `CpoeEntry`; whole-visit / FHIR = future debt
- Patient card `GET /api/patients/[id]/card-summary` → `intakeChecklist` lists auto analyses and auto diagnostics from the current package template after the first care-team doctor. It does not use a fixed four-slot Nafta list and does not wait for `ProgramInstance`. Live: `applyPackageAutoBlocks`. Opening a course does not create orders. The first care-team doctor (`CARE_TEAM`) books every `AUTO_ON_OPEN` and `AUTO_DAY1` block from the current template even when `ProgramInstance` does not exist yet. `MANUAL_RETRY` (super-admin refresh) copies assign mode, kind, and fulfillment onto an existing course snapshot without changing night quotas, then creates the same missing auto orders. ECG/USG blocks marked Auto book `CARDIO-ECG` / `USG-ABD`. Card: anamnesis, complaints, ICD-10, and that checklist after the first doctor; the package itself opens only when anamnesis, one complaint, and one ICD-10 are all present; package procedures and schedule use the same three gates; results and exam notes only when they have rows.
- POST|DELETE /api/sanatorium/episodes/[id]/confirm-no-package — ops signal «guest has no package»; DELETE undoes it, and a new `ProgramInstance` clears it automatically
- POST /api/sanatorium/episodes/[id]/package-apply — manual auto-apply retry (`PENDING_DOCTOR`)
- Cutover report: `scripts/nafta-cutover/rebuild-intake.cjs` (cards `slices.diagnostics`); map `src/lib/import/nafta-intake-map.ts`

## ICD-10 catalog (CLI-39…42)

Global WHO ICD-10 (2019) table `IcdCode` — **no** `organizationId`. Search `GET /api/icd` (selectable CATEGORY/LEAF only; not `/api/icd10`). ADR: [clinic-icd10-catalog.md](../../../docs/adr/clinic-icd10-catalog.md). Optional sync from orchestrator `GET /platform/v1/catalog/icd10` (in-process generator, not data-hub).
